epos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2772298688","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104914#issuecomment-2772298688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104914","id":2772298688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lPevA","user":{"login":"PixelTim","id":181008795,"node_id":"U_kgDOCsn5mw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181008795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim","html_url":"https://github.com/PixelTim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PixelTim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-02T11:42:55Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T11:42:55Z","body":"> This is a documented limitation, see the description of [scale](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_node2d.html#class-node2d-property-scale)\n> \n> Since `global_scale` links to it I'd say it's documented, duplicating the wording introduces the risk of discrepancies between the two\n\nI have read the docs. I is written that:\n\n> Negative X scales in 2D are not decomposable <ins>from the transformation matrix</ins>\n\nBut I'm not using transformation matrix directly to access global scale (`Node2D.global_transform.get_scale()`) , I access it as a property (`Node2D.global_scale`). If Godot uses it internally when calculating `Node2D.global_scale`, then it should be documented below global_position, like this:\n\n> Vector2 global_scale\n>\n> - void set_global_scale(value: Vector2)\n> - Vector2 get_global_scale()\n>\n>Global scale. Negative scales on the X axis will be changed to negative scales on the Y axis and a rotation of 180 degrees. See also scale.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2772298688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2772309645","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104914#issuecomment-2772309645","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104914","id":2772309645,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lPhaN","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-02T11:47:45Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T11:47:45Z","body":"That could be made a bit clearer, but it applies to all assignments 